{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu1t1RHv1APmLH4mnKqC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: make the fix now. Don't wait for a survey.**\n\nYou already have stronger evidence than a survey would give you. The logs show what customers actually do, and the cause is specific: part numbers typed with different formatting. A satisfaction survey would take weeks, get a low and biased response, and couldn't change the decision. It would probably just tell you \"search could be better.\"\n\n**Why it's worth doing:**\n- Three days of engineering is cheap and easy to undo, for example behind a flag.\n- About 340 support calls a month is real sales and support time. Some customers who can't find a part never call; they just buy from someone else.\n- Trade buyers who search by part number usually know exactly what they want. These are high-intent searches you're failing.\n\n**Check first (about half a day):**\n1. **Do the part numbers exist in your data?** Take the top 50 zero-result terms, strip the dashes and spaces by hand, and see how many match a product. If many don't match, you're missing supplier cross-references. That's a data problem, not a matching problem, and the three-day estimate is wrong.\n2. **Will stripping punctuation make different parts look the same?** Check how many distinct parts end up identical after normalising. Handle any you find.\n\n**Measure the result:** record the zero-result rate, search-to-basket conversion and \"can't find part online\" call volume before and after the change. Ideally run it as an A/B test or a staged rollout.\n\n**For the head of sales:** they're right to want customer input, just not as a precondition here. Run the survey afterwards to find the next problem. Their team's call logs are a large part of why this fix is clearly justified."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3189,"cache_read_input_tokens":5035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3189},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9f5288b-e41c-41ba-8953-356dfdf04d95","uuid":"815b1339-32e5-4c93-af93-4e18197bb54c","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:18:02.360Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu1t18RjuLbASzZDg2Z4"}
